**Fixed** — commit `79224aa40`. `js/common/smProvider.js:554` now delegates:

```js
function _ghRawMergeStateStatus(pr) {
    if (!pr) return null;
    return mergeStateReconcile.normalizeMergeStateStatus(
        pr.mergeStateStatus || pr.mergeable_state || null);
}
```

The hand-rolled twin is gone; the "never a fabricated verdict" chain (trim → uppercase → empty→null, String-coerced, null/undefined-guarded) is defined in exactly one place, and the hoisted `require('./mergeStateReconcile.js')` (gh-823) was already in this file. The delegation contract is pinned by a new module-level test — *"non-string garbage normalizes via String() — the shared contract every caller delegates to"* — so a future hardening tweak to the shared normalizer cannot silently skip this call site (your drift scenario).

Behavior-identical: the existing prStatus REST-fallback tests (`no reported state → no reconcile`, `unstable → red`) pass unchanged; full suite on this head 9057/9057.
